      "examples": [
        {
          "code": "LayoutBuilder(builder: (context, constraints) {\n  final roomy = constraints.maxWidth >= 840;\n  return roomy\n      ? Row(children: [navigationRail, Expanded(child: longContent)])\n      : Column(children: [Expanded(child: longContent), navigationBar]);\n});",
          "description": "Original adaptation sketch using SDK primitives; constraints, labels and content come from the host app.",
          "language": "dart"
        }
      ],
      "guidance": "Use the pinned Home.didChangeDependencies width logic and navigation composition as a study, not a fixed device-size recipe. Test 200% text, long localized destination labels and real lists; retain Android 48dp and iOS 44pt effective touch targets. On a narrow foldable cover window keep one task and bottom navigation; on an unfolded/tablet window promote navigation to a rail and expand only content that benefits. Width alone does not detect a hinge: this selected Flutter sample provides no verified hinge avoidance or watchOS support. Prefer constraints from the actual app window, preserve selection on resize, and suppress the navigation transition when reduced motion is requested. Source code is BSD-3-Clause; the full upstream LICENSE also contains third-party font and Apache notices, preserved without copying fonts or images.",
      "id": "github-mobile-flutter-samples",
      "license": "BSD-3-Clause",
      "license_path": "licenses/github-mobile/flutter-samples/LICENSE.txt",
      "platforms": [
        "flutter",
