          "code": "val showTwoPanes = when (widthClass) {\n    Compact -> false // narrow cover or split-screen window\n    Medium -> separatingHinge != null\n    Expanded -> true\n}\n// Supply observed display features to the pane container; never position a control on the hinge.",
          "description": "Original policy sketch for app design; sample identifiers/types are host-provided, not a compiled standalone snippet.",
          "language": "kotlin"
        }
      ],
      "guidance": "Reuse the distinction between window width and device posture. A narrow cover screen remains single-pane even on a foldable; an unfolded or tablet window can expose list and detail while keeping message selection stable. The selected ReplyApp inspects FoldingFeature and ReplyListContent passes displayFeatures to TwoPane, rather than treating the hinge as extra margin. Keep controls and text outside the separating bounds. Test half-open book posture, rotation, split-screen resizing, long messages, 200% font scale and 48dp effective touch targets. This pinned implementation uses Accompanist TwoPane; study its behavior but review current AndroidX adaptive APIs for a new app instead of claiming that this snapshot is the latest architecture. No build or runtime-safety verification was performed.",
      "id": "github-mobile-compose-reply",
      "license": "Apache-2.0",
      "license_path": "licenses/github-mobile/compose-reply/LICENSE.txt",
      "platforms": [
        "android",
