      "guidance": "Keep a readable status such as Loading weather visible independently of the shimmer. On a small Apple Watch show one stable placeholder rather than a dense phone-style skeleton, preserve legibility under enlarged text, and maintain usable approximately 44pt controls where relevant. Disable animation for Reduce Motion and low-power/Always On reduced-luminance contexts using APIs available on the target watchOS version. Limit repeated animation to active foreground loading and expose success, failure and retry without motion-only meaning. Crown scrolling belongs to the containing watch screen, not this effect: test the real long status/list and Digital Crown interaction separately. The repository is not archived, but its last recorded push is August 2024; this is a pinned reference, not a claim of active maintenance or current-device testing.",
